@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the states of an implementation issue in the implementation stage.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: action [guard] / what cumin does. A gray state belongs to another area.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits until the repository can take another issue

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the Implementer works

state "checking" as Checking #EEEEEE
Checking : (the check area)

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee answers

[*] --> Ready : an Assignee adds ready
Ready --> Implementing : request the implementation\n[an Assignee added ready, the repository can take another issue,\nno owner-task, and: the blockers are closed,\nor the only open blocker is not merged yet (IMPL-008.1)]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer
Implementing --> Checking : wait for the checks\n[the Implementer run has ended, the implementation is complete]\n/ cumin links the pull request if needed
Implementing --> Implementing : request the implementation again\n[the Implementer run has ended, the implementation is not complete,\nno question, first time]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer again
Implementing --> Decision : stop the implementation\n[the Implementer run has ended, and: the Implementer asked,\nor the implementation is not complete after the retry,\nor the conflict resolution changed nothing]\n/ cumin notifies
Decision --> Ready : the Assignee adds ready

@enduml
